//RS /// Run one command that must reject the cyclic graph, and return the single
//RS /// `E3502` line that names the chain.
//RS ///
//RS /// Only the programmable build path evaluates `fn build` and validates the
//RS /// graph it returns (`jet build`, and `jet inspect graph` for the
//RS /// no-execution variant). The default `jet run` lens compiles and runs the
//RS /// selected runtime program straight through the JIT — the native execution
//RS /// workflow hands it to `Interpreter::run_jit_once_*`, which only seeds build
//RS /// facts —
//RS /// so `jet run` never walks a build graph and can never observe this fault.
